What accessibility enhancements were the most challenging to implement, and why?
  I'm intimidated by rem conversions. This project has easy ones but I know it won't always be that way. 
  Not using aria until absolutely necessary. 
  The do's and don'ts of Skip Navigation will take me a bit more practive to get a better understanding. 
  

How do ARIA attributes improve the experience for users relying on assistive technologies?
  I'd explain it as decluttering. ARIA simplies pages by removing unwanted, confusing, and unnessary items but also neatly
  organizes pages by making menues, buttons, tab interfaces, form submissions etc. 

What tools did you use to check color contrast, and how did they help?
  I utilized https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/ which I preferred over Ctrl shift C. That is something I'm looking forward to exploring more. 
  The above site helped me hone in on the best colors possible (and was pretty fun playing around with it and thinking about color theory.)
